rl":"/en/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Install and choose an entry point\" href=\"/en/docs/getting-started/installation\" description=\"Start with the smallest package boundary that fits your application.\" />"},"12":{"id":"/en/docs-10","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Build your first store\" href=\"/en/docs/getting-started/quick-start\" description=\"Create state, a cached getter, an action, and a React component.\" />"},"13":{"id":"/en/docs-11","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Understand the state model\" href=\"/en/docs/concepts/state-and-actions\" description=\"Learn the immutable boundary, fixed schema, subscriptions, and lifecycle.\" />"},"14":{"id":"/en/docs-12","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Scale into shared mode\" href=\"/en/docs/shared/overview\" description=\"Move execution into a Worker or SharedWorker without inventing a second authority.\" />"},"15":{"id":"/en/docs-13","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#why-coaction","content":"Coaction is most useful when an application has selector-heavy components, repeated derived\nstate, or a likely path toward worker-backed state. Instead of assembling independent tracking,\ncomputed, immutable-update, and selector plugins, Coaction connects those concerns through one\nreactive graph."},"16":{"id":"/en/docs-14","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#why-coaction","content":"That cohesion has a cost. Zustand remains smaller and more mature, and its explicit selector\nmodel is often exactly right for a small store. Coaction's differentiation is concentrated in\n`observer()`, cached getters, natural `this`-bound actions, and the optional shared runtime—not\nin claiming every store should be more complicated."},"17":{"id":"/en/docs-15","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"Goal"},"18":{"id":"/en/docs-16","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"Start with"},"19":{"id":"/en/docs-17","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"Vanilla, local-only state"},"20":{"id":"/en/docs-18","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"`coaction`"},"21":{"id":"/en/docs-19","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"React with automatic render tracking"},"22":{"id":"/en/docs-20","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"`coaction` + `@coaction/react`"},"23":{"id":"/en/docs-21","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"Vue, Angular, Svelte, or Solid"},"24":{"id":"/en/docs-22","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"The matching `@coaction/*` framework package"},"25":{"id":"/en/docs-23","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"Worker or SharedWorker authority"},"26":{"id":"/en/docs-24","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"`coaction/shared` or a framework package with `worker`"},"27":{"id":"/en/docs-25","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"Keep an existing Zustand/MobX/Pinia/etc. runtime"},"28":{"id":"/en/docs-26","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"The matching whole-store adapter"},"29":{"id":"/en/docs-27","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"Synchronize Coaction-owned state through Yjs"},"30":{"id":"/en/docs-28","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-your-path","content":"`@coaction/yjs` on the owning store"},"31":{"id"