e into getters"],[84,"3\\. Use explicit selectors when they are clearer"],[278,"4.0 import"],[231,"4\\. Decide whether namespaced slices help"],[85,"4\\. Use the imperative store API outside React"],[232,"5\\. Replace middleware separately"],[233,"6\\. Keep Zustand underneath when that is safer"],[234,"7\\. Add shared mode last"],[717,"A copy of the initial state, shaped like the factory's object"],[667,"A curated reference for create options, store methods, types, lifecycle helpers, and isolated entry points."],[614,"A dedicated Worker gives one page its own authority lifetime:"],[167,"A deep-partial object merges known fields. Passing `null` is a no-op. Application code should\nnormally keep updates in named store methods; direct `setState()` is useful for integration,\ntests, and controlled imperative updates."],[223,"A durable outbox, a rebase against a server, offline recovery — `@coaction/sync`."],[499,"a Firestore collection or query, with optional `onSnapshot`"],[349,"A form here, a counter there, one settings panel. Coaction's readonly state and reactive runtime\nmay cost more than those needs justify. The default `coaction` and `@coaction/react` entries\nexclude the shared transport runtime; using a local store does not bundle an inactive transport.\n**Consider Zustand, Jotai, or component state** when their smaller model covers the problem.\nCoaction's local runtime becomes useful when shared derivation or read tracking removes\nsubstantial application code, even if the application never needs a Worker."],[224,"A local store can synchronize with a server without ever creating a Worker. And\na shared store's mirrors are views of one authority, not replicas that diverge\nand get merged — which is what the same vocabulary means in most other\nlibraries."],[497,"a Postgres table, with an optional changes-since cursor and realtime"],[759,"A recipe may also assign that complete value. Use `store.apply(nextState)` when replacing a\ncyclic root, and do not mutate