e `set()` throws the engine's `TypeError` in strict-mode code and is\nsilently ignored in sloppy-mode scripts, instead of throwing Coaction's direct-mutation error.\n`getInitialState()` returns a copy of the initial state shaped like the factory's object, the\nsame object on every call, rather than the factory's object itself. `@coaction/react` adds opt-in\nwhole selectors, `useStore(selector, { whole: true })`, whose selector receives the store's own\ndata and must never mutate it. An array's state is its elements: `create()` and `setState({ ... })`\nleave out its named keys and symbols, as a recipe's first write to it always did, and warn once in\ndevelopment, so keep such a value in an object beside the array. The\nrepository guide\ncompares each change with 4.1."],[102,"Accessor getters"],[242,"Accessor getters are cached. Use `get(deps, selector)` only when explicit dependencies make the\ncode clearer."],[546,"action arguments;"],[592,"action discovery and remote method execution;"],[161,"Actions stay bound"],[371,"Adapter"],[831,"Adapter"],[294,"Adapter authors must leave `store.apply` owned by Coaction and provide\n`internal.externalApply` for their runtime writer. Middleware should use\nStoreCommit hooks to observe all supported transitions,\nincluding writes that do not pass through `apply`."],[674,"Adapter entry"],[419,"Adapters used to replace `store.apply` outright. That took on commit semantics\nthey did not want, and discarded anything middleware had wrapped `apply` with,\nsince middleware runs first."],[640,"Add an external adapter"],[447,"Add diagnostics, persistence, and undo/redo to a Coaction-owned store through middleware."],[661,"Add the shared binder contract suite and type expectations."],[788,"After a transition commits"],[259,"After local tests pass, create the same source on a worker authority and connect a client.\nSwitch the `create` import to the shared entry; the default React entry rejects worker options:"],[830,"All adapters bind a whole store. Slices mode is unsupported for every adapter."],[534,"Always release old bindings to prevent duplicate observers and stale writes."],[567,"Ambiguous graphs"],[631,"An action response includes the authority epoch and resulting sequence. The client waits for its\nmirror to catch up before resolving the action promise. If the incremental update does not arrive\nwithin `executeSyncTimeoutMs` (default `1500` ms), the client falls back to full sync."],[502,"An adapter is two functions, so a backend not listed here is a `pull` and a\n`push`:"],[418,"An adapter that only wants to refuse a direct write, because its runtime takes\nchanges through its own channel, needs no writer at all — refuse from\n`internal.assertMutationAllowed` and let the ordinary `apply` do the work."],[124,"An age change must rerun this selector because it replaces the `user` object, even though the\nname is unchanged. `identity()` returns the same readonly object; `whole()` instead returns\nowned raw data for coarse scans, which must never be mutated."],[369,"An external-state adapter bridges a complete third-party runtime into Coaction. The external\nruntime keeps its native mutation and derived-state semantics; Coaction supplies its store,\nframework, lifecycle, and—for supported adapters—shared method-execution surface."],[337,"An honest boundary check — the situations where Coaction is the wrong tool, and where it has no real competitor."],[151,"An object whose enumerable values are all functions is ambiguous: it could be a method-only\nsingle store or a map of slice factories. Development builds warn when `auto` encounters this\nshape. Make the intent explicit:"],[58,"Angular"],[426,"Angular"],[796,"Any of these registrations requests patch generation while active, even without\n`enablePatches: true`. Each returns an idempotent unsubscribe function. Destroying the store\nreleases registrations; registering after destruction throws."],[784,"API"],[726,"Application code should prefer named actions over `apply()`. `apply()` is a low-level contract for\ntransports, middleware, and adapters."],[627,"applies only the next sequence for that epoch;"],[739,"Are getters recomputed on every read?"],[125,"Array elements are values rather than readonly proxies. An element read by index, found by a\nscan or returned by a getter is the frozen element itself, so it compares equal however it was\nreached, and an object also held at an object key has one identity across both. Reading an\nelement depends on its identity: any write inside an element gives it a new identity, while\nwrites to its siblings do not. A write to an element outside `set()` throws a\n`TypeError` in strict-mode code and is silently ignored in sloppy-mode scripts; either way the\nstate is unchanged."],[326,"Array elements are values: a reader depends on the identity of each element it reads, and array\nmethods such as `filter` and `map` take one dependency on the array. An `observer()` rendering\n`todos[0].title` re-renders after any write inside `todos[0]`, and one rendering a scan after a\nwrite to any element. A selector returning the field or the scan's result reruns, but re-renders\nonly when that result changes."],[126,"Array methods that read every element without changing it, such as `filter`, `map`, `find`,\n`reduce`, `slice` and `for...of`, take one dependency on the array and run over the array itself.\nReads of other state inside the callback are tracked as usual. Use `whole()` for traversals that\nare not a single array method, such as an indexed loop or the values of a record."],[596,"atomic full-snapshot recovery;"],[260,"Audit the state against the strict JSON contract and change call sites to await actions. Direct\nclient `setState()` is not a supported migration shortcut."],[367,"Authoring an adapter"],[613,"Authority changes during an action"],[601,"authorization policy for requests reaching the authority;"],[77,"Authors of external-store adapters and low-level middleware"],[92,"Automatic tracking is optional:"],[612,"Awaiting action visibility"],[491,"Backend"],[481,"Backends"],[791,"Before a transition commits"],[514,"Bind Coaction-owned pure state to a Y.Doc and let a Yjs provider handle peer transport."],[532,"Bind the owning store only; a client mirror must not create a second collaboration authority."],[370,"Binder-backed adapters are not native slices. Never mount an adapted external\nstore below a Coaction slice key."],[552,"booleans and strings;"],[293,"Both `store.apply(nextState)` and `store.apply(base, patches)` publish commits. With patches,\nthe base must be current: omit it with `apply(undefined, patches)` or use `getPureState()`.\nA wrong base throws before changing state or publishing a commit."],[325,"Both `useStore(selector)` and `observer()` use managed deep path tracking on native immutable\nstores. A reader of `state.user.name` can stay cached after an age-only recipe update. Selectors\nstill compare their results with `Object.is`; `observer()` collects reads during render without\nrequiring a selector. Measure selector executions and render counts separately."],[783,"Both forms of `store.apply` publish commits. A listener also sees supported transitions that\nnever go through `apply`. Patches may replace a changed top-level field, or use a full root\nsnapshot at `path: []` for local graphs. A commit pair is not necessarily JSON-serializable;\nshared transport and remote sync impose their own stricter value contracts."],[727,"Both forms publish a commit, so a transition made this way is visible to\n`onStoreCommit` and to everything built on it — history, sync, a devtool. With\npatches, `state` must be the state the store holds: omit it, or pass\n`getPureState()`. A patch pair describes a change to the current state, so\napplying it to a different base would leave the store somewhere its own commits\ndo not lead, and that is refused."],[142,"Boundaries"],[698,"Build a client transport from a worker instance"],[2,"