ld or\nthe scan's result through a selector, which re-renders only when its result changes. Objects\nreached through object keys are tracked as before."],[619,"Coaction cannot catch an exception thrown while your code evaluates `new SharedWorker(...)` before\n`create()` is called. Catch that constructor failure yourself only when local fallback is an\nacceptable product decision. A worker or transport that exists but fails during setup is surfaced\nas an error rather than silently changing the authority model."],[236,"Coaction deliberately keeps a familiar `create()` shape, but a migration is more than changing\nan import. Move one behavior at a time and keep tests green between steps."],[1,"Coaction documentation"],[257,"Coaction does not currently promise a Redux DevTools-compatible built-in experience. Keep\nproject-specific diagnostics or use logger until a maintained DevTools surface exists."],[165,"Coaction exposes a readonly public state. Actions may read through `this`, but all writes to\nCoaction-owned state must happen inside `set()`:"],[6,"Coaction is a Zustand-style state library with three pieces designed to work as one system:"],[15,"Coaction is most useful when an application has selector-heavy components, repeated derived\nstate, or a likely path toward worker-backed state. Instead of assembling independent tracking,\ncomputed, immutable-update, and selector plugins, Coaction connects those concerns through one\nreactive graph."],[246,"Coaction path"],[168,"Coaction records the public shape during initialization. A single store cannot add unknown\ntop-level keys later. A slice store cannot add new slices or new top-level fields inside a\nslice."],[556,"Coaction rejects values that JSON cannot preserve without semantic loss:"],[44,"Coaction requires Node.js 22 or newer for repository development. Published runtime packages are\ninstalled from npm with the package manager you already use."],[585,"Coaction shared mode keeps a single mutation authority. A Worker, SharedWorker, or custom\ntransport can host the main store; page runtimes hold client mirrors."],[112,"Coaction's computed values use the same signal graph as field tracking. A component can read a\ncached getter, that getter can read store fields, and invalidation flows through the graph without\nmanual memo arrays."],[754,"Coaction's public state is immutable. Write inside `set()` so the runtime can commit state,\ninvalidate computed values, notify subscribers, and produce patches when required."],[809,"Combination"],[771,"Commit hooks are for history, persistence, synchronization and other integrations. Application\ncode normally writes through named actions and reads through framework subscriptions.\nImport these hooks from `coaction/adapter`, including when the store was created from a\ndefault local entry."],[797,"Commit listeners run before ordinary subscriptions and effects. A reentrant write completes\ndelivery of the preceding commit before changing state again. Observer errors reach the caller\nafter commit and subscription delivery; they do not roll back an accepted transition."],[302,"Commit patches follow Mutative 2: nested patches come before their parents, and a moved draft\nis carried by the patches of its parent. They replay to the same state, so only tests that\ncompare patch arrays need new expectations. In production, errors from Mutative read\n`Minified Mutative error #<code>`; match the code, and define `process.env.NODE_ENV` in every\nbundle. The repository guide\ncovers loading without a bundler and the draft checks of development builds."],[760,"Commit replay and history preserve the recorded result, using snapshots when necessary. They\ndo not extend the draft editing contract, and shared transport still requires a JSON tree."],[768,"Commit shape"],[129,"Comparison is independent of dependency selection and runs without collecting dependencies.\nEven when a result is reused, branch dependencies are reconciled. The comparator must