citly undefined option is accepted for feature detection and SSR.\nLocal imports exclude the shared transport runtime from the bundle."],[46,"The default entry is the single-context runtime. No transport is reachable from\nit, so the JSON protocol, epoch, reconnect and transport runtime stay out of the\nbundle entirely."],[528,"The default key is `coaction:${store.name}`."],[10,"The default path is intentionally local and synchronous. Shared workers, multiple tabs, and\ncollaboration are capabilities you opt into when the architecture calls for them."],[455,"The default storage is `localStorage` when available. `createJSONStorage()` adapts another Web\nStorage instance, and a custom `PersistStorage` may be synchronous or asynchronous."],[413,"The external runtime owns its mutable object. Unknown root properties written directly onto a\nmutable adapter are not promoted into Coaction's fixed raw/public schema."],[676,"The factory receives:"],[203,"The main store executes actions, commits state, emits ordered patches, and serves full snapshots."],[802,"The maintained combinations for native stores, external adapters, middleware, and Yjs."],[24,"The matching `@coaction/*` framework package"],[28,"The matching whole-store adapter"],[521,"The middleware creates a `Y.Doc`, binds the store, and connects cleanup to `store.destroy()`."],[291,"The old `coaction/local` and `@coaction/react/local` aliases are gone. Shared stores that\npreviously used a default entry must switch to `/shared`:"],[121,"The optional `coaction/derived` entry adds store-owned cached reads without changing native\ngetter defaults or adding this runtime to the default entry's consumer bundle:"],[506,"The outbox, the optimistic snapshot and the adapter's view of the remote are all\nstored as JSON, so state JSON cannot represent is not persisted — it is quietly\nchanged. A `Date` comes back a string; a `Map` comes back `{}`."],[206,"The package exposes static boundaries so a bundler can avoid loading unrelated runtime code:"],[512,"The package README\ncovers the durable checkpoint format, what each built-in adapter guarantees\nunder replay, and the CRUD baseline."],[33,"The public root schema is fixed after initialization; keep dynamic keys inside a declared\nobject or array field."],[160,"The root schema is fixed"],[544,"The rule applies to:"],[184,"The same public store contract appears in three runtime modes."],[116,"The second argument passed to a store factory can declare dependencies manually:"],[442,"The selector call returns a readable Svelte store."],[436,"The selector is handed the store's own data: read it, never mutate it. Keep each hook call in one\nmode, since switching a call between `{ whole: true }` and a tracked selector changes the hooks it\nruns."],[443,"The selector result is a Solid accessor."],[93,"The selector runs inside a reactive tracker, so the paths it reads become its dependencies: a\nwrite that touches none of them does not re-run it at all. `Object.is` still decides the\nre-render, but most writes never reach the comparison. For frequently reused field selectors,\ncreate a cached selector map once:"],[577,"The strict JSON contract applies only when state crosses a shared boundary. A local store may\nhold richer application values, subject to the normal immutable state model. If a store might\nmove into a worker later, keeping its data JSON-shaped from the beginning makes that migration\npredictable."],[368,"The write boundary"],[510,"There is no silent fallback to memory: a runtime with nowhere durable to write\nis refused, because the outbox surviving a crash is the reason it exists."],[414,"These packages expose `bind*` helpers and, where needed, an `adapt()` wrapper:"],[216,"They compose, and none of them implies another:"],[87,"This example uses React because it shows state creation and render tracking in one place. The\nunderlying store model is the same in every framework."],[650,"This freshness check also runs in `pnpm check` and CI. It does not check hand-written\nsemantics or catalog completeness. README, repository guides and the website's two languages\nare separate sources; update matching claims and examples together. The\ndocumentation map\nlists the related surfaces and website checks."],[348,"This guide is deliberately anti-marketing. If your situation is listed under \"skip it\", skip it —\nthe Coaction you would need is not the Coaction being offered."],[488,"This is not shared authority. A synced store owns\nits state and reconciles with a remote; a shared store's mirrors are views of\none authority in another JavaScript context. They compose, and neither implies\nthe other."],[172,"This makes `this` actions safe to pass to event handlers or destructure. Do not use arrow\nfunctions when the action needs `this`; arrow functions capture lexical `this`."],[31,"This site documents Coaction 3.x. A shared authority and every client\nconnected to it must use the same Coaction major and wire protocol."],[314,"This static boundary excludes shared protocol, epoch, reconnect, and transport modules from the\nentry. Use `coaction/shared` for the shared runtime, or `@coaction/react/shared` in React.\nThe default React entry, `@coaction/react`, also stays local."],[183,"Three things the word \"sync\" gets used for"],[321,"Thresholds must not be lowered merely to make a failing run green. A threshold change needs a\nreviewed runtime-semantic or benchmark-methodology reason."],[792,"Throw to refuse a write"],[104,"Tracking granularity"],[108,"Transactions, ownership and React"],[335,"Treat benchmark floors as regression detection and rerun publishable numbers on the target\nmachine."],[591,"TypeScript models this client shape with `StoreWithAsyncFunction`/`Asyncify`: methods become\npromise-returning while data fields remain readable from the local mirror."],[178,"Understand local stores, shared authorities, client mirrors, and Coaction's isolated package boundaries."],[309,"Understand the derived-state tradeoff"],[624,"Unexpected action errors are redacted to `Remote action failed`. The original error remains on\nthe authority. Treat policy code as trusted application code and keep it side-effect free where\npossible."],[571,"Unsafe keys/paths"],[399,"Unsupported"],[409,"Unsupported"],[825,"Unsupported"],[828,"Unsupported"],[853,"Unsupported"],[861,"Unsupported"],[875,"Unsupported"],[879,"Unsupported"],[883,"Unsupported"],[269,"Update shared imports, check integration contracts, keep local React applications on supported versions, and check the Mutative 2 changes of 4.1 and the array element changes of 4.2."],[662,"Update the support matrix and package README in the same change."],[862,"Update through actor events; `setState()` blocked"],[277,"Usage"],[258,"Use `@coaction/zustand` when the existing Zustand store is itself public API, other modules\ndepend on it directly, or replacing ownership would create more risk than value. The adapter is a\nwhole-store integration; it cannot live inside native Coaction slices."],[332,"Use `observer()` where it removes real selector composition."],[113,"Use a normal getter for the default derived-state experience:"],[516,"Use an existing Y.Doc"],[331,"Use cached getters for repeated derived reads, not side-effectful work."],[580,"Use one authority and any number of local mirrors across Workers, SharedWorkers, or custom transports."],[156,"Use slices when namespaces clarify ownership. A small store does not need to be split merely to\nimitate a folder structure."],[47,"Use the shared entry when state crosses a Worker, SharedWorker, or injected transport boundary:"],[117,"Use this form when dependency declaration makes cross-slice logic clearer, or when integration\ncode should not rely on implicit getter reads."],[412,"Use this path when the Zustand store must remain public API or other modules still consume it\ndirectly. For a new store owned by Coaction, prefer the native state model."],[798,"Validators must not write to the store. Throwing rejects a Coaction-mediated transition before\nit changes state. A direct mutation of an external mutable instance has already happened by\nthe time Coaction observes it, so validation cannot veto that mutation. Prepare listeners are\nan integration hook for object graph handling, not a general validation hook."],[401,"Valtio"],[855,"Valtio"],[40,"Vanilla applications"],[279,"Vanilla local store"],[281,"Vanilla shared authority or client"],[19,"Vanilla, local-only state"],[533,"Very large or highly volatile trees can generate substantial update traffic."],[55,"Vue"],[425,"Vue"],[23,"Vue, Angular, Svelte, or Solid"],[702,"Wait before action catch-up falls back to full sync; default `1500`"],[217,"What it is"],[583,"What the application still owns"],[582,"What the runtime handles"],[504,"When a pull brings a change that overlaps something still pending, the default\nkeeps the local write. `conflict: 'remote-wins'` keeps the remote one, and a\nfunction decides per mutation:"],[785,"When it runs"],[336,"When not to use Coaction"],[749,"When should I choose Zustand instead?"],[711,"Whether the input was materialized as slices"],[219,"Which components re-render when a field changes — `observer`, selectors, computed getters."],[794,"While preparing an object-valued transition"],[423,"Whole selectors"],[653,"whole-store adapter: an external runtime owns state;"],[655,"Whole-store adapters use `defineExternalStoreAdapter()` from `coaction/adapter`."],[3,"Why Coaction"],[740,"Why did a direct mutation throw?"],[742,"Why does my client action return a promise?"],[743,"Why was my shared value rejected even though JSON.stringify works?"],[657,"Wire subscriptions and lifecycle in `handleStore`."],[145,"With React, `observer()` tracks the slice fields read during render:"],[91,"Without `observer()`, calling `useCounter()` subscribes to the whole store. That behavior is\nuseful when the store is small or a component intentionally observes everything."],[2